# Docker build-context exclusions for the benchmark stack (which uses the lattice repo
# root as build context for the simulator's silo and api images). Exclude bin/obj/test
# artefacts so docker build doesn't ship gigabytes of compile output into the daemon.
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/.vs/
**/.vscode/
**/.idea/
**/.azurite/
**/*.user
.git/
.github/
**/TestResults/
**/coverage*/
**/results-*.json
benchmark/grafana/dashboards/
benchmark/.run/

# Source-only build contexts: no Dockerfile in this repo needs these trees, and
# packing them is what makes `az acr build` / `docker build` uploads slow.
.scratch/
.tmp/
logs/
artifacts/
BenchmarkDotNet.Artifacts/
docs/
test/
**/*.log

# Local-only artefact trees. These are gitignored, so they are invisible to a
# `git status` sanity check but are very much visible to the build daemon: on a
# working clone `.deploy/` alone reached ~19 GB of volume and image tarballs,
# which a repo-root-context build would upload in full before running a single
# instruction. `.run/` holds per-run benchmark state written while a rig is up.
.deploy/
**/node_modules/
**/.run/